  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q19-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "19",
    "prompt": "Find $x$ if $\\log_3(\\log_9 x)=\\log_9(\\log_3 x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=81$.\n\nChange both logarithm bases to 3 and let $t=\\log_3 x$.",
      "worked": "The outer logarithms require $x>1$. Let $t=\\log_3 x>0$, so $\\log_9 x=\\dfrac{t}{2}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_3\\left(\\frac{t}{2}\\right)&=\\frac12\\log_3 t\\\\\\log_3 t-\\log_3 2&=\\frac12\\log_3 t\\\\\\frac12\\log_3 t&=\\log_3 2\\\\\\log_3 t&=2\\log_3 2\\\\\\log_3 t&=\\log_3 4\\\\t&=4\\\\\\log_3 x&=4\\\\x&=81.\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck: $\\log_3(\\log_9 81)=\\log_3 2$ and $\\log_9(\\log_3 81)=\\log_9 4=\\log_3 2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 72
  },
